		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance linked investment]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.artemis.bm/?p=150604</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Higher short-term interest rates are providing an additional source of return for ILS, while also reshaping strategy-level return attribution across the hedge fund industry. As macroeconomic dynamics shift which management styles deliver relative performance, Don Steinbrugge, of Agecroft Partners, emphasises that the underlying source of an investment&#8217;s return now matters just as much as its [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/higher-short-term-rates-boost-ils-returns-reshape-hedge-fund-attribution-agecrofts-steinbrugge/">Higher short-term rates boost ILS returns, reshape hedge fund attribution: Agecroft’s Steinbrugge</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
